# Admin UI efficiency (Razor Pages)

Intranet admin consoles must feel instant. Prefer partial updates over full page rebuilds.

## Row / micro actions

- Prefer **small dedicated POST forms** or **`fetch` + JSON** for single-row actions (Approve, Set, Ping, Probe, Enroll).
- Do **not** put row actions inside a giant SaveAll form via `formaction` — that posts every field and hits `FormOptions.ValueCountLimit` (HTTP 400 once N ≳ 150).
- Keep bulk-edit fields **`disabled` until Edit mode** so accidental submits omit them (see Discovery).
- Match existing AJAX patterns: `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest`, antiforgery token, `{ ok, message, … }` JSON; fall back to redirect for non-JS.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD — tiny POST, optional AJAX
public async Task<IActionResult> OnPostApproveAsync(int id) {
    // mutate one row…
    if (WantsAjax()) return new JsonResult(new { ok = true, id, removeRow = true, message });
    TempData["SkipDiscoveryBackfill"] = "1";
    return RedirectToPage(/* filters only */);
}
```

## Expensive GETs after POSTs

- After a micro-action, **do not** re-run catalog backfill, discovery-key scans, fleet aggregates, or full list HTML when a toast + one-row DOM update suffices.
- Gate heavy work: skip with TempData flags, tab-scoped `LoadAsync`, or section/host query params.
- Never auto-run `BackfillFromDiscoveriesAsync` (or similar full reprocess) on every GET — use an explicit operator button.

## List-page query cost

On Discovery, App Lists, Remote Machines, Enrollment / Historical Dashboard, Machines:

- Ask: does this click need the **entire** catalog, all ProcessRuns, or period aggregates?
- Avoid N+1 and “load all assignments to change one name”.
- Prefer `AsNoTracking` for read paths; count/filter in SQL when lists grow.

## Forms & ValueCountLimit

- Program raises `FormOptions.ValueCountLimit`, but still design so row actions stay **O(1) fields**, not O(rows).
- Bulk Save is OK as a deliberate Edit → Save flow; do not reuse it for Approve/Set/Ping.

## UX bar

- Single Approve / Set / Ping / Test RDP should feel **sub-second** on the same machine as the API.
- Bulk ops: Prefer **AJAX batches** for Approve all (chunk size ~40). Full reload is OK for Save all / Import CSV.
